Z||000000||vinnywolfe||07-19-2000||11:01 PM||||i read a thread a while ago where a member suggested removing the plastic "restrictor" plate, located behind the plastic grill on the air intake, to improve airflow.  is this a good idea?<BR>seems like it was put there for a reason (controlled leak for airflow)?<BR>just wondering.  went to take it out today and after inspecting it, decided to ask first.<P>thanks,<P>vinny<BR> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||FIEROCIOUS||07-20-2000||02:38 AM||||I'ts there to prevent monsoon rains from entering the engine and to silence some noise. I took mine out about a year ago and no problems. The one thing I don't like but live with happily is it does make a audible hissss at certain RPMs.<P>Also you can modify your air filter canister by removeing the center post triangle and install clips from a first gen RX7 air cleaner on top. Then bolt the bottom of the canister to the bracket connected to the frame. (Not for unmechanicaly inclined) ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||07-20-2000||04:03 AM||||I plan on removing the whole assembly, and doing a ram air intake with a K&N, and ducting the side scoop (mecham style) right into it..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>There should be some performance increases, as well as a cool hissing sound...<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
